title: Government on the verge of collapse
subtitle: The current [+ cat_coalition_disp +] may very well be living its last days.
new-page: true
face-image: img/events/government_breakup.webp
tags: event
role: event
view-if: coalition_rupture_trigger
on-arrival: coalition_rupture_trigger = false
call: generalitat_coalition_card.prepare
go-to: options

@options
on-arrival: {!
    var target = Q.coalition_rupture_target;
    Q.coalition_rupture_relations = Q[target + "_relations"];
    Q.coalition_rupture_expulsion = target == Q.president_party;
    Q.coalition_affairs_concession_target = target;
    Q.coalition_affairs_indy_demand = Q.coalition_affairs_indy_demands[target];
    Q.coalition_rupture_indy_available = !!Q.coalition_affairs_indy_demand;
    var reasonPrefix = "coalition_affairs_indy_" + (target == Q.parlament_current_ciu ? "ciu" : target);
    for (var reason of ["pending", "aligned", "no_roadmap", "faction_blocked", "consultations_passed", "referendum_passed", "no_law"]) {
        Q["coalition_rupture_indy_" + reason] = !!Q[reasonPrefix + "_" + reason];
    }
    if (!["erc", "cup", Q.parlament_current_ciu, "jxsi", "jxcat"].includes(target)) {
        Q.coalition_rupture_indy_no_roadmap = true;
        Q.coalition_rupture_indy_no_law = true;
    }
    Q.coalition_rupture_policy_right = ["ciu", "cdc", "dl", "pdcat", "junts", "jxsi", "jxcat"].includes(target)
        || (Q[target + "_ideology"] || "").includes("Conservatism");
    var canLeft = Q.tax_policy_level >= -2 && Q.tax_policy_level < 2 || Q.economy_cuts > 0;
    for (var field of ["education_spending", "healthcare_spending", "public_salary_level"]) {
        if (Q[field] >= -2 && Q[field] < 2 && Q[field] + 1 <= Q.social_spending_cap) canLeft = true;
    }
    var canRight = Q.generalitat_surplus < 0 || Q.tax_policy_level > -2;
    Q.coalition_rupture_policy_available = Q.coalition_rupture_policy_right ? canRight : canLeft;
    // PSC's random policy route must have a deliverable outcome on either branch.
    if (target == "psc") Q.coalition_rupture_policy_available = canRight && canLeft;
    Q.coalition_rupture_resource_gain = Q.difficulty < 0 ? 5 : 3;
    if (Q.coalition_affairs_indy_demand) {
        Q.coalition_affairs_indy_kind = Q.coalition_affairs_indy_demand.kind;
        Q.coalition_affairs_indy_roadmap = Q.coalition_affairs_indy_demand.roadmap || 0;
        Q.coalition_affairs_indy_law = Q.coalition_affairs_indy_demand.law || "";
    }
!}

= Government on the verge of collapse

After many disagreements since the start of the legislature, our relations with [+ coalition_rupture_target +] are at an all time low. So much so, that right now they [? if coalition_rupture_expulsion: intend to expel us from the government! ?][? if not coalition_rupture_expulsion: intends to withdraw from the government! ?][? if coalition_rupture_low_relations: Relations have deteriorated just way past beyond what they are willing to tolerate. ?][? if coalition_rupture_broken_agreement: We have failed to acquiesce with the agreement we reached with them. ?][? if coalition_rupture_roadmap_conflict: Our roadmaps to independence differ too much. ?]

- @policy
- @independence
- @resources
- @elections
- @leave

@policy
title: Offer policy concessions to preserve the coalition
subtitle: This may be our last resort to avoid a government breakup
choose-if: coalition_rupture_policy_available and coalition_rupture_relations + 8 >= 40
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not coalition_rupture_policy_available: No deliverable policy concession possible that would satisfy their needs. ?][? if coalition_rupture_relations + 8 < 40: This is simply not enough to calm their dissent. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.coalition_affairs_concession_target = Q.coalition_rupture_target;
    Q.coalition_rupture_random = G.random(Q);
!}
go-to: policy_right if coalition_rupture_policy_right or (coalition_rupture_target = "psc" and coalition_rupture_random <= 0.5); policy_left

@policy_right
call: generalitat_coalition_card.concessions_ciu
go-to: saved_policy

@policy_left
call: generalitat_coalition_card.concessions_icv
go-to: saved_policy

@saved_policy
call: generalitat_setpolicy
go-to: saved

@independence
title: Offer independence concessions to preserve the coalition
subtitle: This may be our last resort to avoid a government breakup. [? if coalition_rupture_indy_available: [? if coalition_affairs_indy_kind = "roadmap": We'll adopt a [+ coalition_affairs_indy_roadmap : roadmap +] roadmap.?][? if coalition_affairs_indy_kind = "law": Commit to passing the [? if coalition_affairs_indy_law = "parlament_non_binding_consultations": Law on Non-Binding Consultations?][? if coalition_affairs_indy_law = "parlament_referendum_law": Law on the Referendum?] within a year.?]?]
choose-if: coalition_rupture_indy_available and coalition_rupture_relations + 8 >= 40
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not coalition_rupture_indy_available: [? if coalition_rupture_indy_pending: We already owe this partner further strides towards independence... ?][? if not coalition_rupture_indy_pending: [? if coalition_rupture_indy_aligned: Our roadmaps are already aligned. ?][? if coalition_rupture_indy_no_roadmap: Our current roadmaps are just too different. ?][? if not coalition_rupture_indy_aligned and not coalition_rupture_indy_no_roadmap: [? if player_in_jxsi or player_in_jxcat: We cannot change our party's roadmap separately while in a unity list. ?][? if consultation_pending or referendum_pending: A vote on independence is pending already! ?][? if congreso_decidir_countdown > 0 and player_roadmap < 2: We must wait for the Congreso's right-to-decide vote before we can reasonably chance our stance on independence. ?][? if not player_roadmap_change_trigger: We have changed our roadmap too recently. ?][? if coalition_rupture_indy_faction_blocked: Our current party's internal power dynamics block the necessary roadmap changes. ?]?][? if coalition_rupture_indy_no_law: No possible commitment to independence seems to be available at the moment that would satisfy them. ?][? if not coalition_rupture_indy_no_law and not parlament_sovereignty_declaration: A parliamentary Declaration of Sovereignty is required before any further steps towards independence can be made. ?][? if coalition_rupture_indy_consultations_passed: The Law on Non-Binding Consultations has already been passed. ?][? if coalition_rupture_indy_referendum_passed: The Law on the Referendum has already been passed. ?]?]?][? if coalition_rupture_relations + 8 < 40: This is simply not enough to calm their dissent. ?]
call: generalitat_coalition_card.accept_independence
go-to: saved

@resources
title: Mobilize our party to preserve the coalition
subtitle: This will require significant effort on our side. \[-3 resources\]
view-if: difficulty < 1
choose-if: party_resources >= 3 and coalition_rupture_relations + coalition_rupture_resource_gain >= 40
unavailable-subtitle: [? if party_resources < 3: Not enough resources. ?][? if coalition_rupture_relations + coalition_rupture_resource_gain < 40: This is simply not enough to calm their dissent. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.party_resources -= 3;
    Q[Q.coalition_rupture_target + "_relations"] += Q.coalition_rupture_resource_gain;
!}
go-to: saved

@saved
on-arrival: {!
    Q.coalition_rupture_recheck = true;
    // A direct arrival must not report success for an undelivered concession.
    Q.coalition_rupture_saved = Q[Q.coalition_rupture_target + "_relations"] >= 40;
!}
go-to: leave if not coalition_rupture_saved

Against all predictions, it seems like the current [+ cat_coalition_disp +] will live to fight another day. So far, it seems like [+ coalition_rupture_target +] has accepted our concessions, but we better watch out in the future...

@elections
title: Call a snap election instead!
subtitle: It may be time to let the voters decide instead.
choose-if: (player_in_jxsi and president_party == "jxsi") or (player_in_jxcat and president_party == "jxcat") or (player_party == president_party)
unavailable-subtitle: We do not control the Presidency.
on-arrival: {!
    Q[Q.coalition_rupture_target + "_relations"] += 3;
!}
go-to: snap_election

@leave
title: [? if coalition_rupture_expulsion: We've been expelled from the Generalitat?][? if not coalition_rupture_expulsion: [+ coalition_rupture_target +] withdraws from the Generalitat ?]
subtitle: There is nothing we can do.
on-arrival: {!
    var vehicle = Q.player_in_jxsi ? "jxsi" : Q.player_in_jxcat ? "jxcat" : Q.player_party;
    var target = Q.coalition_rupture_target;
    var removed = [target == Q.president_party ? vehicle : target];
    var ciuFamily = ["ciu", "cdc", "dl", "pdcat", "junts"];
    if (removed.includes("erc") && Q.cat_coalition.includes("cup") && Q.cat_coalition.some(function(p) { return ciuFamily.includes(p); })) {
        removed.push("cup");
    }
    Q.coalition_rupture_removed = removed.join(", ");
    Q.cat_coalition = Q.cat_coalition.filter(function(p) { return !removed.includes(p); });
    Q.cat_coalition_support = (Q.cat_coalition_support || []).filter(function(p) { return !removed.includes(p); });
    Q.cat_coalition_abstain = (Q.cat_coalition_abstain || []).filter(function(p) { return !removed.includes(p); });
    var belongs = function(p, parties) {
        return parties.includes(p) || ["jxsi", "jxcat"].some(function(list) { return parties.includes(list) && Q[p + "_in_" + list]; });
    };
    for (var party of Q.parties) {
        Q[party + "_in_gob"] = belongs(party, Q.cat_coalition);
        Q[party + "_supporting"] = Q[party + "_in_gob"] || belongs(party, Q.cat_coalition_support);
    }
    G.setText(Q, "position_disp", (belongs(Q.player_party, Q.cat_coalition) ? G.text("Generalitat") : G.text("<span style='font-style: italic'>Opposition</span>")));
    if (!belongs(Q.player_party, Q.cat_coalition)) {
        Q.burdens_time = 0;
        Q.burdens_goal = 0;
        Q.burdens_pending_points = 0;
        Q.burdens_start_trigger = false;
        Q.burdens_start_countdown = 0;
        Q.countdowns = Q.countdowns.filter(function(id) { return id != "burdens_start"; });
    }
    for (var record of Q.coalition_indy_commitments || []) {
        if (removed.includes(record.target) || removed.includes(vehicle)) record.status = "retired";
    }
    for (var record of Q.coalition_policy_commitments || []) {
        if (!(record.signatories || []).some(function(p) { return removed.includes(p); })) continue;
        record.status = "retired";
        G.deactivateLaw(Q, "coalition_pending_" + record.kind, undefined, true);
    }
    var seats = Q.cat_coalition.reduce(function(total, p) { return total + (Q[p + "_parlament_s"] || 0); }, 0);
    var strength = seats >= Q.parlament_s_majority ? "Majority government" : "Minority government";
    G.setText(Q, "cat_coalition_disp", G.governmentTooltipText("generalitat", Q.cat_coalition, (strength === "Majority government" ? G.text("Majority government - {seats}/{majority}", {
        seats: String(seats),
        majority: String(Q.parlament_s_majority)
    }) : G.text("Minority government - {seats}/{majority}", {
        seats: String(seats),
        majority: String(Q.parlament_s_majority)
    })), G.text("{parties} {government}", {
        parties: String(Q.cat_coalition.join("–")),
        government: (strength === "Majority government" ? G.text("majority government") : G.text("minority government"))
    })));
    Q.coalition_rupture_preserved_offices = {};
    var offices = {president: "president", vp: "vicepresident", economy: "economy_minister", interior: "interior_minister", health: "health_minister", education: "education_minister", territory: "territory_minister", foreign: "foreign_minister", bnl: "bnl_minister"};
    for (var key in offices) {
        var office = offices[key];
        var replacement = removed.includes(Q[office + "_party"]);
        Q["parlament_coalition_proposal_" + key] = replacement ? Q.president_party : Q[office + "_party"];
        if (!replacement) Q.coalition_rupture_preserved_offices[key] = {party: Q[office + "_party"], name: Q[office], gender: Q[office + "_gender"]};
    }
    Q.coalition_rupture_recheck = true;
!}
call: parlament_coalition_setnames
go-to: reshuffled

@reshuffled
on-arrival: {!
    var offices = {president: "president", vp: "vicepresident", economy: "economy_minister", interior: "interior_minister", health: "health_minister", education: "education_minister", territory: "territory_minister", foreign: "foreign_minister", bnl: "bnl_minister"};
    for (var key in offices) {
        var office = offices[key];
        var saved = Q.coalition_rupture_preserved_offices[key];
        Q[office + "_party"] = saved ? saved.party : Q["parlament_coalition_proposal_" + key];
        Q[office] = saved ? saved.name : Q["parlament_coalition_proposal_" + key + "_name"];
        Q[office + "_gender"] = saved ? saved.gender : Q["parlament_coalition_proposal_" + key + "_gender"];
    }
    G.setText(Q, "historical_event", G.text("{coalition_rupture_removed} left the Generalitat government after a coalition rupture. {president} continues to lead {cat_coalition_disp}.", {
        coalition_rupture_removed: String(Q.coalition_rupture_removed),
        president: String(Q.president),
        president_gender: Q.president_gender,
        cat_coalition_disp: G.getText(Q, "cat_coalition_disp")
    }));
!}

With [+ coalition_rupture_removed +] out of the government, the Generalitat is now under a [+ cat_coalition_disp +]. We'll have to see how long this lasts...
 
